     <message name="IDS_AUTOFILL_AI_LOCAL_SAVE_NOTIFICATION_TITLE" desc="The title of an informational dialog. This dialog appears when a user attempts to save data (like a driver's license) to Google Wallet, but the request fails (e.g., due to server error or connection issues). The title clarifies that the information was not lost, but rather saved locally to the device instead.">
       Info saved to device only
     </message>
-    <message name="IDS_AUTOFILL_AI_LOCAL_SAVE_NOTIFICATION_DESCRIPTION" desc="The body text of an informational dialog. The user sees this after a failed attempt to save to Google Wallet. 'Couldn't save...' acknowledges the server failure. 'Saved to Chrome...' confirms the safety of the data (local fallback). 'Chrome will offer...' sets expectations that the system will retry the cloud save the next time this data is accessed.">
-      Couldn't save this info to your Google Wallet. It's saved to Chrome on this device instead. Chrome will offer to save it to Wallet next time you use it.
